            <div xml:id="d465">

                <pb facs="0697" n="585" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg585"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 1296/7.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Jackson to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-09-23"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 23, 1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 583 Greek Series.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence, I
                    have the honor to transmit copies of Nos. 122 and 131 of the Greek Official
                    Gazette, which contain the text of the extradition treaties<anchor n="a"
                        xml:id="d465-f1"/> negotiated by Greece Avith France (March 29–April 11,
                    1906) and Germany (February 27–March 12, 1907), respectively, and to be sir,
                    etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John B. Jackson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
